                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6bab14b3-1785-3de7-8622-96b86a00aead",
                        "entry_id": "231ae160-65ab-3c5b-9a51-f80af17c7c56",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pratique utilisée par des scénaristes ou des producteurs de médias pour attirer l’attention d’une audience queer via « des allusions, des blagues et des symboles homo-érotiques suggérant une relation non-hétérosexuelle entre deux personnages, qui est par la suite réfutée et dénigrée. »"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Anglicism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1251339a-2165-4b79-9b0e-01f762d576a2",
                                "sense_id": "6bab14b3-1785-3de7-8622-96b86a00aead",
                                "text": "Cette pratique, que les spécialistes appellent le queerbaiting, consiste à mettre en place des stratégies de marketing et de communication pour draguer l’audience queer."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bf3b2d36-1365-4629-a113-552856c075e5",
                        "source_entry_id": "231ae160-65ab-3c5b-9a51-f80af17c7c56",
                        "source_sense_id": "6bab14b3-1785-3de7-8622-96b86a00aead",
                        "target_lang_word": "queerbaiting",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "queerbaiting",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "833e6670-290e-3821-a37f-34a84b510b72",
                                        "entry_id": "dbbc9983-8f9b-384b-9de5-89c5d0df54b0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The practice of creating homoerotic tension between two characters in a narrative work (particularly a television series) without the intention of ever developing it into an actual same-sex relationship or explicitly addressing the question of either character's sexuality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca0cf50e-c8f6-4797-a70e-b6e603ec57aa",
                                                "sense_id": "833e6670-290e-3821-a37f-34a84b510b72",
                                                "text": "Queerbaiting is erasure. It’s telling queer people that they don’t exist, or that our stories aren’t worth telling, and it’s harmful."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c30881f-658e-428b-a76a-552c80bede0c",
                                                "sense_id": "833e6670-290e-3821-a37f-34a84b510b72",
                                                "text": "Some feel that fan pressure to emphasize Buffy and Spike’s relationship spoiled the last few seasons of Joss Whedon’s show, and many fans were alienated by Teen Wolf’s recent queer-baiting."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d002754-5598-40cd-8206-fe70fc88389d",
                                                "sense_id": "833e6670-290e-3821-a37f-34a84b510b72",
                                                "text": "Criticism of queerbaiting also does not imply that creators need to be dictated to by fans on how to run their show; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "630bc277-5442-4703-981b-3b564bdb49bf",
                                                "sense_id": "833e6670-290e-3821-a37f-34a84b510b72",
                                                "text": "And as a much better NYT comment piece on queerbaiting put it last year: “As self-serving as some celebrity caginess can be, you can’t build a world in which everyone feels free to self-identify by ordering everyone to self-identify.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
